---

<div class="hiring-stack">
  <TemplateNotice id="template-notice-heading">
    <p>
      This hiring page is a CV/resume template built for recruiters and hiring
      managers. All quantified outcomes are illustrative placeholder examples
      used to model strong result framing, business-impact language, and
      decision-ready storytelling.
    </p>
    <p>
      World-class recipe: make each bullet answer four questions in one line:
      <strong>What was owned?</strong>
      <strong>What changed?</strong>{' '}
      <strong>How much did it improve?</strong>
      <strong>Why did the business care?</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      Replace placeholders with verified outcomes in this order:
      <strong>revenue/cost impact</strong>, <strong>reliability impact</strong>, <strong
        >delivery speed</strong
      >, then <strong>scope of ownership</strong>. Include before/after deltas,
      timeframe, and operating context.
    </p>
    <p>
      Credibility rules: quantify with metrics tied to P&L or risk, keep claims
      attributable to your direct ownership, and remove generic strengths not
      backed by evidence. If a claim cannot be measured, frame it as scope, not
      outcome.
    </p>
    <p>
      Evidence model: every highlighted material metric should map to an
      auditable reference source.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="cta-secondary" href="/evidence">Open Evidence Registry</a>
    </p>
  </TemplateNotice>

  <section class="mode-hero" aria-labelledby="hiring-heading">
    <div class="headline-row">
      <span class="headline-icon" aria-hidden="true"
        ><Briefcase size={86} /></span
      >
      <h1 id="hiring-heading">
        Senior .NET backend engineer driving reliability and delivery outcomes
        in production systems.
      </h1>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-row">
      {
        roleEmailCtas.hiring.map((cta) => (
          <EmailCta cta={cta} mode={visitorModes.hiring} />
        ))
      }
      <PageShareButton
        shareRole="Recruiter / Hiring Manager"
        label="Share with hiring team"
        source="hiring_hero_cta"
        shareTitle="Robertas Rudys | Recruiter / Hiring Manager"
        shareText="Sharing this profile for backend hiring review."
      />
    </div>
    <noscript>
      <p class="cta-note">
        Email links require JavaScript. Please enable JavaScript to contact me.
      </p>
    </noscript>
    <p class="cta-note">
      Hiring for an open backend role: request the resume or schedule a short
      intro.
    </p>
  </section>

  <PeerSharePrompt
    message="Forward this profile to one teammate hiring for backend product engineering."
  />

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="hiring-summary">
    <h2 id="hiring-summary">Profile Snapshot</h2>
    <p>
      Senior .NET backend engineer for production teams, leading API and service
      delivery from scoped requirements through release.
    </p>
    <p>
      Recent outcomes in high-use systems:{' '}
      <ProofFact
        text="13 to 9 day lead time, 34% fewer Sev-2/3 incidents, and 68% to 88% on-time roadmap delivery"
        title="Cross-Role Snapshot References"
        refs={[
          'Lead-Time Dashboard (Release Cycles, baseline vs. current)',
          'Incident and Hotfix Trends (quarter-over-quarter)',
          'Roadmap On-Time Delivery Review (quarterly planning cadence)',
        ]}
        href="/evidence#snapshot"
        hrefLabel="View in Evidence Registry"
      />
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="hiring-scope-kpis">
    <h2 id="hiring-scope-kpis">Core Scope & Reliability KPIs</h2>
    <p>
      Scope and KPI ownership across high-concurrency adtech, enterprise
      internal systems, and mature .NET product services.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Backend scope: C#, .NET, ASP.NET Core, REST APIs, and service
        integration boundaries in existing systems.
      </li>
      <li>
        Data-path scope: SQL schema/query design, bottleneck removal, and
        production tuning.
      </li>
      <li>
        Reliability scope: incident triage, safe refactors, legacy debugging,
        change-risk reduction, and operational hardening.
      </li>
      <li>
        Delivery scope: cross-functional planning with product/data partners,
        peer review, and CI/CD-ready releases.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      KPI track record:{' '}
      <ProofFact
        text="99.90% -> 99.95% availability, 12% -> 7% change-failure rate, 46% fewer outage minutes, 0 minutes unplanned downtime across two release trains"
        title="Reliability KPI References"
        refs={[
          'SLO Availability Reports (pre/post release hardening)',
          'Change-Failure Rate by Release (baseline vs. current)',
          'Outage Minutes and Downtime Logs (two release trains)',
        ]}
        href="/evidence#reliability"
        hrefLabel="View in Evidence Registry"
      />
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hiring-stack {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.95rem;
    }

    .hiring-stack > section {
      margin: 0;
    }
  </style>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="hiring-experience">
    <h2 id="hiring-experience">Experience Highlights</h2>
    <p>
      Role evidence focused on direct ownership and measured business outcomes.
    </p>
    {
      hiringExperience.map((role) => (
        <article>
          <h3>{role.title}</h3>
          <p>
            {role.company} | {role.period}
          </p>
          <ul>
            {role.details.map((item) => (
              <li>
                {item.lead}
                <ProofFact
                  text={item.metric}
                  title={item.proof.title}
                  refs={item.proof.refs}
                  href={item.proof.href}
                  hrefLabel={item.proof.hrefLabel}
                />
                {item.tail}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <section class="card" aria-labelledby="hiring-availability">
    <h2 id="hiring-availability">Hiring Readiness</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Target role:</strong> Senior backend engineer for API delivery, service
        reliability, and release outcomes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Work model:</strong> Remote-first, EU-time-zone overlap, direct access
        to product and engineering decision-makers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fast process:</strong> Align first-quarter scope, success KPIs, interview
        stages, and compensation band before final round.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Confirm early:</strong> Employment setup, overlap hours, on-call expectations,
        and start date.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Strong fit:</strong> Backend modernization work with explicit reliability
        and delivery goals.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not a fit:</strong> Undefined ownership, constant fire-fighting, or
        unclear hiring process constraints.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
